extends layout

block content
  .row.banner
    .col-12
      h1= title
  .row
    .col-12.col-lg-8 
      p Enthusiasm and Motivation: <br><br>
      ul
        li| A Rating of 1 - Speaker shows little to no interest in the topic presented. <br><br>
        li| A Rating of 2 - Speaker shows some negativity during the presentation. <br><br>
        li| A Rating of 3 - Speaker shows some positive feeling and personal engagement with the subject, but not particularly enthusiastic. Motivates some audience interest and/or curiosity. <br><br> 
        li| A Rating of 4 - Speaker demonstrates strong positive feeling about the subject throughout the presentation. Motivates interest; sparks curiosity; audience feels they have learned something.<br><br>
      p Elocution: <br><br>
      ul
        li| A Rating of 1 - The speaker mumbles, incorrectly pronounces many terms, and speaks too quietly or too fast for people in the back to hear.<br><br>
        li| A Rating of 2 - The speaker’s voice is low or speaks too quickly, and incorrectly pronounces a few terms. Audience members have some difficulty hearing.<br><br>
        li| A Rating of 3 - The speaker’s voice is clear. The speaker pronounces most words correctly, and speaks neither too quickly nor too slowly. Most audience members can hear clearly.<br><br> 
        li| A Rating of 4 - The speaker speaks with a clear, measured voice with precise pronunciation so that all audience can hear and understand the presentation.<br><br>
      p Vocalized Pauses: <br><br>
      ul
        li| A Rating of 1 - Extreme (and distracting) overuse of vocalized pauses. <br><br>
        li| A Rating of 2 - Vocalized pauses are noticably distracting. <br><br>
        li| A Rating of 3 - Vocalized pauses are occasional but not disruptive or distracting. <br><br> 
        li| A Rating of 4 - Very few noticable Vocalized pauses.
        <br><br>
             
             
      .col-12.col-md-12 
        button.btn.btn-primary.float-left 
          a(href="/evaluation/skills") Go Back to Rating         